  cd /tmp/instr && patch -p1 < <repo>/docs/measurements/m2.10-4-cycle-timing.patch
  cargo build --release --locked --offline -p signal-cli --target-dir /tmp/instr-target
  SIGNAL_PROF_SECTION=<s> /tmp/instr-target/release/signal render <loop project> \
    --seconds 5 --threads 1 --out /tmp/out

It times, with std::time::Instant, one section per run (SIGNAL_PROF_SECTION,
0 to 8, listed in prof.rs) of whole_unit's cycle branch and whole_direct (the
one-thread path), for one-frame calls only, and prints the total, the count
and the mean at the end of `signal render`. Section 8 is an empty section:
the timer's own cost, subtracted from the others. docs/benchmarks.md, "The
cost of cycle units", gives the method, the projects and the results.

